{
  "name": "Run a Telegram AI assistant with long-term memory using past.dev and OpenAI",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Telegram AI assistant with long-term memory\n\nFor people who want a personal or team assistant in Telegram that still knows next month what you told it today.\n\n### How it works\n- A Telegram message starts the workflow.\n- The AI Agent calls past.dev **Recall** as a tool when it needs something from earlier conversations. It gets the facts with their dates and sources.\n- Simple Memory keeps the flow of the current chat.\n- The answer goes back to Telegram.\n- The question and the answer are saved to past.dev, so the next session knows about them.\n\n### Setup\n1. Self-hosted n8n: open **Settings > Community Nodes**, select **Install** and enter `n8n-nodes-pastdotdev` (tested with 0.1.0 on n8n 2.47). [Installation guide](https://docs.n8n.io/integrations/community-nodes/installation/)\n2. Create a project API key in the [past.dev console](https://app.past.dev) and add it as a **Past Dev API** credential in each past.dev node.\n3. Add your Telegram bot token (from @BotFather) and your OpenAI credential.\n4. In **Receive Telegram message**, restrict the bot to your own user IDs.\n\n### Customization\n- Change the system message in **Answer with memory**.\n- Use another chat model.\n- Without an Audience, every user of the bot reads the same project memory. For private memory per user, set an Audience in **Save the exchange to memory**.\n",
        "height": 760,
        "width": 460,
        "color": 1
      },
      "id": "766ba381-f3b6-5710-85f4-bd885be1e0b7",
      "name": "Sticky Note Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -760,
        -420
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Receive the message\nOnly text messages continue.",
        "height": 300,
        "width": 440,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "b1dd34e0-06e2-5aab-8aa6-8cd474803148",
      "name": "Sticky Note A",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -260,
        -120
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Answer with memory\nThe model writes the recall query. The identity always comes from Telegram, never from the model.",
        "height": 520,
        "width": 560,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "c1b0b39c-abb9-5cee-9593-65cceabda2a4",
      "name": "Sticky Note B",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        220,
        -120
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Reply and remember\nSend the answer, then save the exchange with its real time and a stable Source ID.",
        "height": 300,
        "width": 480,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "612fa393-c96d-502d-9379-1ef61f180bd3",
      "name": "Sticky Note C",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        820,
        -120
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "**Restrict the bot.** Add your Telegram user IDs in this node, or anyone who finds the bot can read the memory.",
        "height": 150,
        "width": 210,
        "color": 3
      },
      "id": "70f97001-d236-5b10-bff2-b129e004870b",
      "name": "Sticky Note Warn",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -250,
        190
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "updates": [
          "message"
        ],
        "additionalFields": {}
      },
      "id": "98c8971d-0090-5e76-8459-6d29c01784e7",
      "name": "Receive Telegram message",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.telegramTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1.2,
      "position": [
        -200,
        0
      ],
      "webhookId": "c09a8061-68eb-563c-9bab-d2a9539f91ec"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "caseSensitive": true,
            "leftValue": "",
            "typeValidation": "loose",
            "version": 2
          },
          "conditions": [
            {
              "id": "147e7898-206c-5c32-9b47-6850155f1c1d",
              "leftValue": "={{ $json.message.text }}",
              "operator": {
                "type": "string",
                "operation": "notEmpty",
                "singleValue": true
              },
              "rightValue": ""
            }
          ],
          "combinator": "and"
        },
        "looseTypeValidation": true,
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "41828091-e2ac-512d-8582-ed37e36c10cc",
      "name": "Message has text",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "typeVersion": 2.2,
      "position": [
        20,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "={{ $json.message.text }}",
        "options": {
          "systemMessage": "=You are a helpful assistant in Telegram. Today is {{ $now.toFormat('cccc d LLLL yyyy') }}.\n\nYou have a long-term memory. Before you answer a question about the user, earlier conversations, decisions, plans or facts, call the tool \"Recall from past.dev\" with a precise question. Use what it returns, and say when a fact is old. If the memory has nothing, say that you don't know yet. Never invent a memory.\n\nKeep answers short. Use plain text, no Markdown."
        }
      },
      "id": "f9cdba7b-c7a9-5252-8dd4-311d4b6be9d9",
      "name": "Answer with memory",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.agent",
      "typeVersion": 3.1,
      "position": [
        300,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "model": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "list",
          "value": "gpt-4.1-mini"
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "353260d4-fef5-51df-9b5c-bb1453f52686",
      "name": "OpenAI Chat Model",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.lmChatOpenAi",
      "typeVersion": 1.3,
      "position": [
        260,
        220
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "sessionIdType": "customKey",
        "sessionKey": "={{ $('Receive Telegram message').item.json.message.chat.id }}",
        "contextWindowLength": 10
      },
      "id": "206bea11-3e88-57bf-9130-ddac61d2041a",
      "name": "Keep this chat session",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.memoryBufferWindow",
      "typeVersion": 1.3,
      "position": [
        420,
        220
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "descriptionType": "manual",
        "toolDescription": "Recall what is known from long-term memory about the user, earlier conversations, decisions and facts. Give a precise question as the query.",
        "resource": "memory",
        "operation": "recall",
        "query": "={{ $fromAI('query', 'The question to look up in memory', 'string') }}",
        "identity": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "id",
          "value": "={{ 'telegram-' + $('Receive Telegram message').item.json.message.from.id }}"
        },
        "options": {
          "limit": 10
        }
      },
      "id": "90857c04-9823-54b2-9bab-c9ed88a22d06",
      "name": "Recall from past.dev",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-pastdotdev.pastDevTool",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        600,
        220
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "chatId": "={{ $('Receive Telegram message').item.json.message.chat.id }}",
        "text": "={{ $json.output }}",
        "additionalFields": {
          "appendAttribution": false
        }
      },
      "id": "07d1a7b9-05b5-52a1-8f61-50b286ceb76d",
      "name": "Send the answer",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.telegram",
      "typeVersion": 1.2,
      "position": [
        880,
        0
      ],
      "webhookId": "3e221285-959c-5080-954e-6b7c48592c34"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "resource": "memory",
        "operation": "ingest",
        "content": "=User: {{ $('Receive Telegram message').item.json.message.text }}\nAssistant: {{ $('Answer with memory').item.json.output }}",
        "identity": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "id",
          "value": "={{ 'telegram-' + $('Receive Telegram message').item.json.message.from.id }}"
        },
        "additionalFields": {
          "id": "=telegram-{{ $('Receive Telegram message').item.json.message.chat.id }}-{{ $('Receive Telegram message').item.json.message.message_id }}",
          "timestamp": "={{ DateTime.fromSeconds($('Receive Telegram message').item.json.message.date).toUTC().toISO() }}",
          "label": "Telegram conversation"
        }
      },
      "id": "f85caa97-c574-5f55-968b-26b97a66bfce",
      "name": "Save the exchange to memory",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-pastdotdev.pastDev",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1100,
        0
      ],
      "retryOnFail": true,
      "waitBetweenTries": 3000,
      "maxTries": 3
    }
  ],
